# The retired signing key, and the one file in this repository that must never be in it.
#
# The root .gitignore already has *.pfx. This is deliberately the second rule
# rather than a redundant one: the root file is long, general, and edited for
# reasons that have nothing to do with signing, and it only takes one person
# reorganising it to remove the only thing standing between a private key and a
# public repository. This rule sits beside the key it protects, is four lines
# long, and has exactly one reason to be edited.
#
# What the key is: the self-signed certificate releases 1.3.1 to 1.5.x were
# signed with. Nothing builds with it since 2.0.0, which is signed with Azure
# Artifact Signing and keeps no key anywhere near this repository (#793). It
# stays dangerous while any 1.5.x machine still trusts it - anyone holding this
# PFX can sign a package that installs there as an upgrade - so the rule stays
# for as long as a copy of the file might.
devcert.pfx
